Configuration (Environment Variables)

All settings support ENV overrides.

Paths

LOG_FILE (default /var/log/proxmox_maintenance.log)

STATE_DIR (default /var/lib/proxmox_maintenance)

HTML_REPORT (default /tmp/proxmox_dashboard_report.html)

Email

MAIL_TO (required for your environment)

MAIL_FROM (default proxmox@<fqdn>)

MAIL_SUBJECT_PREFIX (default Proxmox Health + Shutdown Report)

Behavior

POWER_OFF_NODE (default 1)
Set 0 to avoid powering off the host.

VM_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT (default 60)

VM_GLOBAL_WAIT (default 600)

PBS Wait

PBS_SAFETY_WAIT (default 900)

PBS_STABLE_CHECKS (default 10)

PBS_INTERVAL (default 5)

Dry Run

DRY_RUN=1 or run with --dry-run

Usage
Dry run (recommended first)
./proxmox-maintenance.sh --dry-run

Run without powering off the node
MAIL_TO="you@example.com" POWER_OFF_NODE=0 ./proxmox-maintenance.sh

Typical unattended run (powers off by default)
MAIL_TO="you@example.com" ./proxmox-maintenance.sh

Mail Transport

The script requires a working sendmail interface.

Option 1: msmtp-mta (lightweight SMTP relay)

Option 2: postfix (local MTA)

See examples/msmtprc.example.

Safety Notes

Default behavior may power off the node. Set POWER_OFF_NODE=0 if you do not want shutdown.

apt dist-upgrade can change kernels and require reboot; plan maintenance windows accordingly.

The emailed report includes the last 200 lines of the maintenance log; treat it as potentially sensitive.
